  "details": "Seen a few old posts asking for a search bar in the avatars tab but I haven't seen any specifically mentioning the Tags system that was implemented/revamped when the Avatar Marketplace was released.\n\nSince all avatars seem to be able to be tagged, regardless of if they're listed on the AVM or not I think it would be useful to add a filtering system to the Avatars Tab which lets you filter by tag in a section (like Uploaded or Favorites) to only show those avatars. \n\nExample: You've uploaded a few avatars with FaceTracking and quickly want to filter to just ones with the \"FaceTracking\" tag so you can show off your FaceTracking.\n\nCould also implement it in a way that includes the content warning tags since they're surfaced close to the tags in both the SDK and on the website.\n\nOn top of filtering by tags, it would be neat if we could also filter for Performance Rank, and Platform Compatibility. These are already exposed on each Avatar Thumbnail but it can be annoying searching through all your uploaded and favorited avatars to find the one you need.\n\nExample: I'm hopping to a performance gated instance where I need to be in a Medium or better avatar. I would like to be able to quickly filter for just those avis so I can quickly switch to one and be on my way.",
